      "writtenOn": "2023-04-01T06:11:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct. For now I decided to make these be always sampleable (or rather ShaderRead) since I don\u0027t imagine many situations in which a storage texture is not eventually read by a shader.\n\nThe one situation I can think of is a storage texture that is rendered to in a compute shader which then only gets used for CPU-readback (so is never read from a subsequent compute or render pass). That feels like a very specific situation, so I wanted to keep the API simple for now.\n\nThough if you strongly feel that we add an additional flag now, I wouldn\u0027t be opposed to it and I can happily add that.",
      "parentUuid": "04431964_ea928e47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 799,
